From 089abfe48435c0983806603a1b6751aff6b0a6f0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gianluca Mazza <info@gianlucamazza.it>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 00:22:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] drm/msm/dsi: phy: 28nm-8960: report the VCO rate that is
 generated

dsi_pll_28nm_clk_set_rate() programs an integer feedback divider, so the
VCO can only run at multiples of 2 * (27 MHz / 27) = 2 MHz. The
determine_rate callback only clamped the requested rate, so the clock
framework assumed the exact requested rate, while recalc_rate later read
back a rate rounded down to the next 2 MHz step.

On the Nexus 7 (2013) the JDI LT070ME05000 panel requests a byte clock
of 116.61975 MHz, i.e. a VCO rate of 932.958 MHz, which the PLL
generates as 932 MHz. Downstream clocks derived from the requested rate
then no longer match the hardware.

Round the rate in determine_rate the same way set_rate programs it.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/phy/dsi_phy_28nm_8960.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/phy/dsi_phy_28nm_8960.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/phy/dsi_phy_28nm_8960.c
index 8dcce95..41bf8af 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/phy/dsi_phy_28nm_8960.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/phy/dsi_phy_28nm_8960.c
@@ -235,10 +235,19 @@ static int dsi_pll_28nm_clk_determine_rate(struct clk_hw *hw,
 					   struct clk_rate_request *req)
 {
 	struct dsi_pll_28nm *pll_28nm = to_pll_28nm(hw);
+	unsigned long step = 2 * (VCO_REF_CLK_RATE / VCO_PREF_DIV_RATIO);
 
 	req->rate = clamp_t(unsigned long, req->rate,
 			    pll_28nm->phy->cfg->min_pll_rate, pll_28nm->phy->cfg->max_pll_rate);
 
+	/*
+	 * The feedback divider programmed by dsi_pll_28nm_clk_set_rate() is
+	 * an integer, so the VCO can only run at multiples of twice the
+	 * pre-divided reference clock. Report the rate that will actually be
+	 * generated, so that consumers derive their rates from it.
+	 */
+	req->rate = rounddown(req->rate, step);
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
